WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.153
You plug in your phone,

00:00:02.153 --> 00:00:03.731
and it stops at 80%.

00:00:03.731 --> 00:00:05.682
Is it broken? Usually not.

00:00:05.682 --> 00:00:08.112
There are three different reasons
it can happen.

00:00:08.281 --> 00:00:10.074
One. A limit you chose.

00:00:10.074 --> 00:00:13.344
Some phones let you set
a charge limit, like 80%.

00:00:13.344 --> 00:00:16.546
The phone charges close to it,
then stops.

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:18.497
Two. A learned routine.

00:00:18.497 --> 00:00:19.812
If you charge overnight,

00:00:19.812 --> 00:00:22.404
the phone can learn
when you usually unplug.

00:00:22.404 --> 00:00:23.300
It waits at 80,

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.972
then finishes just before you wake up.

00:00:26.142 --> 00:00:27.470
Three. Heat.

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:29.735
A battery warms up as it charges.

00:00:29.735 --> 00:00:33.442
If it gets too warm, the phone
may hold it around 80%,

00:00:33.442 --> 00:00:36.038
and continue once it cools down.

00:00:36.253 --> 00:00:38.352
So why protect the battery at all?

00:00:38.352 --> 00:00:41.725
Phone batteries wear faster
when they sit full for a long time,

00:00:41.725 --> 00:00:43.173
and when they get hot.

00:00:43.173 --> 00:00:46.768
Over the years, that wear shrinks
how much the battery can hold.

00:00:46.768 --> 00:00:49.026
Pausing at 80 cuts the time spent full,

00:00:49.026 --> 00:00:51.279
and that helps to slow the wear.

00:00:51.494 --> 00:00:52.562
Need 100% today?

00:00:52.562 --> 00:00:55.398
Your battery settings
let you change it.

00:00:55.398 --> 00:00:57.500
And charge somewhere
it can stay cool.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:00.056
Not under a pillow,
and not in the sun.

00:01:00.271 --> 00:01:02.236
80% is not a fault.

00:01:02.236 --> 00:01:04.730
It’s your phone looking after
its battery.
